<BaseLayout title="About Mr. D and Tension" description="Why Tension exists, who writes it, and how its educational content is created.">
  <article class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 prose">
    <h1>About Tension</h1>
    <p>Tension is a private educational project for adults exploring intentional intimacy and consensual power dynamics—whether they are single, dating, or in an established relationship.</p>
    <h2>About Mr. D</h2>
    <p>Mr. D is a pseudonym used for privacy. The writing combines lived experience, practical frameworks, community knowledge, and published research where relevant. It is educational content, not therapy, medicine, legal advice, or crisis support.</p>
    <p>Using a pseudonym should not mean asking readers for blind trust. Safety-related claims are sourced where evidence exists, uncertainty is stated when research is limited, and corrections are recorded when something changes.</p>
    <h2>What Tension is for</h2>
    <p>The goal is to help adults ask better questions, communicate more clearly, and approach exploration with consent, care, and realistic expectations. No article creates consent, diagnoses an experience, or replaces qualified professional support.</p>
    <p>Questions or corrections: <a href="mailto:hello@tension.app">hello@tension.app</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
